---
vars: [topic]
---
Write a comprehensive report about {{topic}}. Cover the history, the current
state, the main competing views, the economics, the technical constraints, the
regulatory environment, and the likely trajectory over the next five years.
Consider the perspectives of users, operators, regulators, and researchers.
Be thorough. Be precise. Be balanced. Do not omit edge cases. Do not hedge.
Do not use bullet points unless a list is genuinely clearer than prose.
Do not repeat yourself. Do not pad the response. Do not invent facts.
When you are unsure, say so explicitly and explain what would resolve it.
Prefer concrete examples over abstractions. Cite the sources you rely on.
Explain your reasoning before each conclusion. Define every technical term.
Assume the reader is intelligent but new to the domain. Avoid jargon where a
plain word will do, but do not simplify away the details that matter.
Write at least two thousand words and at most two thousand five hundred words.
